    "023-ferry-ordinary-followup": {
      "session": 34,
      "scene": "ch2_riverfront_resolution",
      "latest_exchange": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Mara, is everyone from the tollhouse rescue accounted for, and what work remains before Willowwake can use the crossing again?",
          "event_id": 1436,
          "citations": [],
          "rules_edition": null,
          "ruling_citation_ids": [],
          "turn_id": null,
          "roll_status": null,
          "roll": null,
          "created_at": "2026-10-23T12:08:08.590392Z"
        },
        {
          "role": "dm",
          "content": "Mara checks the slate in her hand, then answers plainly. \u201cJory Fen is home. We have no other rescued person identified as still missing.\u201d\n\nJory stands with her near the landing, while the secured grain barge rests against the pilings. The temporary plan is in effect: people are kept clear of the dangerous ferry berth, and crossings are postponed until the river settles. \u201cThat gives Willowwake a safe precaution for now,\u201d Mara adds. \u201cIt isn\u2019t a working crossing. Later we\u2019ll need to choose whether to repair the ferry with safeguards, pursue another crossing, or continue making temporary arrangements.\u201d\n\nRain threads down the pilings as residents gather their spare coils and boats. What would you like to take up next?",
          "event_id": 1436,
          "citations": [
            {
              "page": 12,
              "source": "the_silent_ferry_preparation_replay_20261022",
