    "025-ferry-occupation": {
      "session": 34,
      "scene": "ch2_riverfront_resolution",
      "latest_exchange": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "Jory, what is your job in Willowwake, and how can you help Mara decide when the crossing can safely reopen?",
          "event_id": 1442,
          "citations": [],
          "rules_edition": null,
          "ruling_citation_ids": [],
          "turn_id": null,
          "roll_status": null,
          "roll": null,
          "created_at": "2026-10-23T12:10:13.654293Z"
        },
        {
          "role": "dm",
          "content": "Jory answers, \u201cI\u2019m Willowwake\u2019s ferryman. River work is my job\u2014getting people across when it\u2019s safe.\u201d His practical, river-worn clothes are still damp from the rescue. He glances toward the secured grain barge, then back to Mara. \u201cI can help you judge the river and organize the ropes and boats. But I can\u2019t give you a safe time to reopen the crossing yet.\u201d\n\nMara taps her slate. \u201cFor now, we keep people clear of the dangerous berth and postpone crossings until the river settles. Jory can advise us as conditions change, but we haven\u2019t established a specific level or sign that makes reopening safe. We\u2019ll need to assess it then, before anyone crosses.\u201d The barge remains secured at the pilings as rain runs in rivulets between them. What would you like to take up with Mara or Jory?",
          "event_id": 1442,
          "citations": [
            {
              "page": 12,
              "source": "the_silent_ferry_preparation_replay_20261022",
              "audience": "player",
